\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The three-body comparison.
\f0\b0  You explicitly stopped on my phrase \'93three-sided problem\'94 and asked: \uc0\u8232 \'93anything like a three-body problem?\'94\uc0\u8232 That was a useful structural idea and I omitted it from the recovery. The value was not simply \'93there are three sides\'94. It was that 
\f1\b UDF, Shakti and the Elvi can have shifting relationships
\f0\b0 , so an action by one changes the relationship between the other two. It was a model for instability, not terminology to put into the prose. It belongs beside the later, stronger observation that 
\f1\b all those systems are becoming unstable at once
\f0\b0 .\uc0\u8232 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The golf course was potentially tactically useful terrain before it became funny social terrain.
\f0\b0  Your original off-page note was that the golf course is within walking distance, would probably be 
\f1\b tactically useful
\f0\b0 , and would be 
\f1\b impinged by the occupation
\f0\b0 . I recovered its proximity and the later camping/golf material but largely dropped this first reason it mattered. The comedy works partly because terrain that might otherwise be useful to an occupying force becomes contaminated\'97socially, legally and practically\'97by golfers, campers, members\'92 children and Elvi.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 You specifically corrected my geographic simplification of the golf course.
\f0\b0  Your point was not merely that \'93the course is nearby\'94. You said:\uc0\u8232 \'93some of the holes of the golf course are much closer to the compound, stretching in real-world as far out as Cliff View Road.\'94\uc0\u8232 That means 
\f1\b the clubhouse distance is misleading for narrative geography
\f0\b0 . The course itself reaches towards the compound. I mentioned this in the recovery but compressed away its significance.\uc0\u8232 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \'93Subsequent arrivals complicate logistics\'94 was an explicit causal thread.
\f0\b0  I allowed this to dissolve into the broader idea that the Elvi change the environment. Your actual point was sharper: the UDF begins with one logistical situation; 
\f1\b every subsequent population arriving makes its practical operation harder
\f0\b0 . That includes checkpoint throughput, usable terrain, civilian movement and the growing impossibility of treating the area as a clean military space. Vehicle movements themselves stay off page; their consequences do not.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Elvi celebration starts innocent in a stronger sense than I recovered.
\f0\b0  You said:\uc0\u8232 \'93Initially the Elvi are there to celebrate.\'94\uc0\u8232 That is important because the later presence of the three stolen Gyges-disc guitars should not retrospectively make the gathering feel like covert military deployment. The celebration is genuinely celebration. The dangerous capability is hidden inside something culturally ordinary.\uc0\u8232 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Rock Against Revival parallel was more specific than \'93youth culture joins in\'94.
\f0\b0  You said the situation had:\uc0\u8232 \'93parallels to the Rock Against Revival while being a development of it.\'94\uc0\u8232 I recovered the generational/class element but not the creative instruction that this should 
\f1\b develop an existing social mechanism in the book rather than merely repeat it
\f0\b0 . Airborne youth culture again becomes materially consequential, but under new circumstances: military occupation, Christmas, Elvi pilgrimage/celebration, inherited wealth and access to mountain property.\uc0\u8232 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The golf club being overwhelmed by members\'92 children is a better mechanism than I allowed the recovery to show.
\f0\b0  Your correction was:\uc0\u8232 \'93more likely they are overwhelmed by children of their members showing up.\'94\uc0\u8232 That is not merely why the club tolerates camping. It is an 
\f1\b inside-access mechanism
\f0\b0 . The institution\'92s own social class undermines its ability to exclude the influx. The children are not random festival-goers asking permission from outside.\uc0\u8232 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Likewise the 16-bedroom mansions are being taken over through social permission, not generic accommodation overflow.
\f0\b0  Your exact idea was:\uc0\u8232 \'93Many Airborne kids visit their \'91friends\'92 in the mountains and effectively take over their friends\'92 parents 16-bedroom mansions.\'94\uc0\u8232 I retained the houses but softened the 
\f1\b \'93effectively take over\'94
\f0\b0  dynamic. That is useful. The parents\'92 enormous private infrastructure gets repurposed by their own children and social networks.\uc0\u8232 \
\ls1\ilvl0
