\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The manuscript, not this conversation, is the style corpus.
\f0\b0  You told me:\uc0\u8232 \'93Look closer at the sentence and paragraph structure of my work (in the Scrivener bundle, not the conversation context)\'94\uc0\u8232 That distinction deserves to be in the recovered constraints. My own prose in this chat has contaminated the context, so 
\f1\b the chat itself is unsafe as the primary style model
\f0\b0 . Your Scrivener First Draft-or-higher prose is the authority for sentence and paragraph architecture.\uc0\u8232 \
