\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The opposite error is also explicitly banned.
\f0\b0  Your original concern was that the long continuous piece:\uc0\u8232 \'93spends too much of the material, and rushes beyond other events in the timeline\'94\uc0\u8232 creating:\uc0\u8232 \'93a false sense of order for the reader.\'94\uc0\u8232 So we have two simultaneous constraints, and neither cancels the other:\uc0\u8232 
